vmhal3d (JHRobotics/vmhal9x 8bc480e): Direct3D flat shading drawn with GL smooth shading when
it makes no difference (build 3119). For each DrawPrimitives2 call MesaDraw6ColorsUniform walks
the command buffer; when every vertex it draws has the same diffuse and specular colour (or
the FVF has none), flat and smooth shading give the same picture and MesaShadeApply sets
GL_SMOOTH for the call. On the G86 (nouveau nv50) the hardware's flat shading gives clipped
triangles a garbage colour: Half-Life's renderer draws everything flat with white vertices
and its near walls, clipped against the screen, came out pure white (corner wedges). Calls
with varying colours, DX8 vertex shaders and commands the walk does not know keep GL_FLAT.
Apply after vmhal3d-ddfifo.patch; the files are CRLF upstream (patch --binary with CRLF hunks,
or strip and restore CR).

